<h2 id="labels" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">3. Learner-facing labels</h2>

**Required** for all suite wireframes and implref plans — full map in v2 **§4.0**.

| Surface | Use |
|---|---|
| Row 1 · tabs · chips | **Lay label (academic)** when a clear academic term exists and space allows — e.g. `Verbs with -se (reflexive)`, row-1 `me, te, se (clitics)` |
| Tight row-1 | Drop `(academic)` on narrow nav; keep full label on tabs/chips |
| Area / tab first screen | One-line intro — expand if parentheses were dropped from the button |
| Routes · slugs · DB | Stable **internal** ids — never the parenthetical |
| How to choose ▾ | User-facing steps — not “Procedure A” on the button |

**Wireframe convention:** show full **UI label** in `[ brackets ]` including `(academic)` where applicable; note slug in route table, e.g. `nav "me, te, se (clitics)" · slug clitics`.

